  "interpretation": [
    "Inside index_topk both modes compute the same function; their distance to the FP32 reference (mean |delta logprob| about 0.0116) is BF16-versus-FP32 numerics.",
    "Beyond index_topk native DSA stays at that level (0.0111 single node, 0.0115 over two nodes), while dense mode drifts (0.0123, maximum 0.22 versus 0.13 native). Dense and native differ from each other 2.4 times more beyond index_topk (0.0120) than inside it (0.0051).",
    "Remaining native-versus-reference differences include FP8 quantization of the indexer queries and keys in vLLM, which the official BF16/FP32 indexer omits, so near-tied keys can be selected differently.",
    "Two layers bound the size of the effect; the full 61-layer model cannot be run in the FP32 CPU reference."
  ]
}
